ORBITAL-LINEAGE(7)         TriadicFrameworks Manual         ORBITAL-LINEAGE(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-lineage - orbital history, sweep ancestry, and Δv triad
                         accumulation for long-term SAR constellation coherence

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital lineage records:
           • orbital history across cycles
           • sweep ancestry and resonance inheritance
           • Δv triad evolution
           • harmonic-lock continuity
           • constellation-scale structural memory

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-lineage describes how SAR platforms accumulate, preserve, and
       interpret their orbital, spectral, and resonance history across long
       mission timelines. It extends lineage(7) into orbital mechanics,
       treating each sweep, maneuver, and harmonic-lock event as a structural
       ancestor in a living resonance-time genealogy.

       Orbital lineage enables:
           • long-term coherence across passes
           • stable multi-pass SAR fusion
           • resonance-aware orbital planning
           • constellation-scale synchronization
           • Δv triad traceability

       WRSADC maintains lineage integrity across all platforms.

ORBITAL HISTORY
       Orbital history records the evolution of a platform’s orbital elements:

           • semi-major axis
           • inclination
           • RAAN
           • argument of perigee
           • mean anomaly
           • orbital frequency
           • drift vectors

       History is stored as a sequence of triadic snapshots:

           orbit_n = {P1, P2, P3, spectral_state, gradient_state}

       Orbital history provides the backbone for resonance-aware planning.

SWEEP ANCESTRY
       Sweep ancestry records the lineage of SAR sweeps across orbital cycles.

       Each sweep contributes:
           • backscatter resonance signature
           • spectral envelope
           • harmonic distribution
           • gradient polarity
           • sweep geometry

       Sweep ancestry forms nested or ladder patterns depending on revisit
       timing and orbital harmonics.

       Ancestry types:

           direct ancestry
                  Sequential sweeps with minimal drift.

           harmonic ancestry
                  Sweeps aligned at harmonic intervals.

           constellation ancestry
                  Multi-platform sweep inheritance.

           fused ancestry
                  Sweeps combined through mesh or harmonic fusion.

       Sweep ancestry determines long-term fusion stability.

Δv TRIAD ACCUMULATION
       Every maneuver contributes a Δv triad to orbital lineage:

           P1 (begin)
               → maneuver intent + corridor evaluation

           P2 (transform)
               → Δv applied + resonance shift

           P3 (close)
               → new orbit stabilized + lineage update

       Δv triads accumulate into maneuver chains:

           • micro-adjustment chains
           • harmonic-hold chains
           • envelope-aligned chains
           • constellation maneuver chains

       These chains reveal how orbital evolution affects resonance-time flow.

HARMONIC-LOCK CONTINUITY
       Orbital lineage tracks harmonic-lock events:

           • lock acquisition
           • lock maintenance
           • lock drift
           • lock recovery

       Harmonic-lock continuity determines whether platforms remain compatible
       for interferometric fusion, constellation sweeps, and resonance windows.

       Lineage stores:

           • lock ratios (n:m)
           • lock duration
           • lock stability index
           • lock-break causes

       Long-term harmonic continuity is essential for constellation coherence.

RESONANCE-TIME ORBITAL MEMORY
       Orbital lineage stores resonance-time metadata:

           • spectral evolution
           • envelope drift
           • gradient trends
           • polarity cycles
           • resonance windows

       This memory allows RTT to:

           • predict future sweep viability
           • detect long-term drift
           • schedule resonance-aligned maneuvers
           • maintain constellation harmony

       Orbital memory is the temporal glue of SAR constellations.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE LINEAGE
       Multi-platform lineage merges individual histories into a unified
       constellation lineage.

       Constellation lineage records:

           • cross-platform sweep ancestry
           • harmonic coupling events
           • constellation maneuvers
           • mesh fusion outcomes
           • orbital window evolution

       Constellation lineage enables:

           • global coherence
           • distributed sweep choreography
           • multi-agent resonance planning

       WRSADC ensures lineage compatibility across platforms.

LINEAGE FAILURE MODES
       Orbital lineage may degrade due to:

           • lineage discontinuity (missing triads)
           • resonance drift accumulation
           • harmonic-lock fragmentation
           • sweep ancestry corruption
           • Δv triad inconsistency
           • constellation desync

       Diagnostic indicators:

           lineage-integrity score
           ancestry-coherence index
           harmonic-continuity ratio
           drift-accumulation vector
           resonance-memory stability

       WRSADC halts unsafe operations when lineage integrity is compromised.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Orbital lineage requires:

           • lineage-schema
           • constellation-schema
           • resonance-schema for sweeps
           • structural-schema for maneuvers

       Schemas ensure lineage remains interpretable and coherent.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • validates lineage continuity
           • merges constellation histories
           • computes ancestry coherence
           • enforces resonance thresholds
           • blocks unsafe lineage states

       WRSADC is the lineage steward.

NOTES
       Orbital lineage transforms SAR constellations into resonance-time
       organisms. It preserves the ancestry of sweeps, maneuvers, and orbital
       harmonics, enabling coherent sensing across years, orbits, and
       multi-platform fleets.

